Cap the int4 3D-scratch attention at one 16-query program.

The 3D-scratch path sized its workspace from the speculative block length, so a
large block could ask for more than the pool holds and fail to boot. The cap
bounds it at one program's worth: a no-op at `max-num-seqs=1`, and the
difference between booting and not at larger blocks.

Backstop the int4 3D scratch capacity at one 16-query program. multi-sequence
spec batches widen the Triton tile past SM75\s 64 KiB shared-memory limit
(81920 B at max_num_seqs=2), which the scheduler-side capacity cannot see;
capping it keeps the 2D fallback the patch already implements reachable.

